in @prism
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens

# @mirror/lens/lsp — the editor lens (LSP transport).
#
# The editor transport per docs/specs/the-convergence.md §1.2. tower-lsp
# adapter; LSP methods on document ranges map to mq expressions scoped
# to document nodes. The audience is an editor (VS Code, Helix,
# Neovim); the surface is LSP-shaped JSON; the algebra is unchanged.
#
# Per docs/specs/the-convergence.md §2.1: every porcelain verb maps to
# an LSP method shape — `mirror compile` is `publishDiagnostics +
# documentSymbol`, `mirror kintsugi` is `codeAction(kind=source.kintsugi)`,
# `mirror reflect` is `hover` over a declaration, etc. The lsp lens IS
# the editor-protocol notation of the same algebra.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Fourth species under @mirror/lens. Transport-side lens; editor
# audience; eigenboard-tagged diagnostics ride on the verdict envelope;
# the daemon stays the regulator (two editors pointed at the same
# project MUST see the same eigenvalue, per the-convergence.md §1.4).
#
# === Body status ===
#
# FAMILY-HEADER ONLY this tick. The action surface declares the LSP
# method shape (translate-from / translate-to between LSP positions
# and substrate refs); bodies (the actual tower-lsp dispatcher, the
# method table, the codeLens / hover / codeAction handlers) land when
# the consumer (the lsp transport binary served by `spectral serve`
# or `mirror serve`) pulls.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/the-convergence.md §2.1,
#               docs/insights/mcp-lsp-unification.md.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]].
# Related shards: lens.mirror (the family root),
#                 lens/cli.mirror, lens/shell.mirror, lens/mcp.mirror.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/lens/lsp.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/lens/lsp` and only that.

# === actions — abstract surface; bodies land on consumer pull ===

# method — declare a LSP method name + its expected arg shape. Per
# the-convergence §2.1: every method maps to one operation in the
# algebra; the method name is the LSP standard name.
method(name, args: ref) -> lsp { \ }

# range_to_ref — translate an LSP range on a document into a substrate
# ref. The verifier rejects ranges that don't resolve to a node.
range_to_ref(doc: ref, range: ref) -> ref { \ }

out @mirror/lens/lsp
out method
out range_to_ref
